    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-flax-retting-separation","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-pubmed-flax-retting","anchor":{"section":"Abstract"},"note":"The article describes retting as separation of bast-fibre bundles from core, epidermis and cuticle through pectin cleavage. It establishes no local flax, water, duration, technique, tool, quality, worker or output.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-cooking-fat-fire-response","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-nfpa-cooking-oil","anchor":{"section":"Safety considerations for cooking with oil"},"note":"NFPA advises turning off heat and covering a pan fire, and leaving the pan covered until cool. It establishes no fire, pan, fuel, flame size, lid, water source, injury or outcome in a scene.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-warp-tension-unevenness","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-handwoven-warp-tension","anchor":{"section":"Causes of Uneven Warp Tension"},"note":"The weaving guidance identifies winding and spacing causes of uneven warp tension. It establishes no loom, thread, textile, defect, adjustment method or successful repair in a scene.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-willow-moisture-flexibility","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-musgrove-willow-soaking","anchor":{"section":"Soaking willow"},"note":"The basketry guidance states that dried willow absorbs water in soaking and becomes flexible for weaving. It establishes no willow species, rods, vessel, soaking duration, basket, worker or successful bend.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-clay-plasticity-selection","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-uaf-clay-plasticity","anchor":{"section":"Plasticity is the essential feature"},"note":"UAF identifies plasticity as essential to forming clay. It establishes no deposit, soil composition, moisture, processing, firing, vessel or suitability of a particular surface mud.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-waterpower-flow-head","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-doe-hydropower-basics","anchor":{"section":"How hydropower works"},"note":"DOE explains that hydropower uses flowing water and that usable power depends on water flow and head. It establishes no mill, wheel, channel, intake, obstruction, season, output or repair.","review_status":"approved"},
    {"schema":"world_knowledge_evidence_v1","evidence_ref":"evidence:macro-b19-pack-load-balance","source_ref":"source:macro-b19-working-equids-loads","anchor":{"section":"Pack animals"},"note":"ICWE says excessive or imbalanced pack loads increase energy expenditure, fatigue and injury risk. It establishes no animal, load, route, weight, saddle, fit, condition, injury or journey outcome.","review_status":"approved"}
